---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import UptimeDefender from '../components/UptimeDefender.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Uptime Defender — Mila Business Solutions LLC"
  description="A small arcade game. You're the firewall: catch data packets, dodge fireballs, keep the shield up."
>
  <Section narrow>
    <div class="reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Coffee break</p>
      <h1 style="margin-top:var(--space-3);">Uptime Defender</h1>
      <p class="lead" style="margin-top:var(--space-4);">
        You're the firewall. Catch the data packets, dodge the fireballs, and
        keep the shield up as things speed up.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section narrow tight>
    <UptimeDefender />
  </Section>

  <Section sunken narrow title="Why is this here?">
    <p>
      Mostly because it was fun to build. But it's also a small, honest
      demonstration: it runs at a steady frame rate on a phone, it works with a
      keyboard or a mouse or a thumb, it pauses itself when you scroll away
      rather than quietly draining your battery, and if you have reduced-motion
      turned on it drops the screen shake and particle effects instead of
      ignoring you.
    </p>
    <p>
      None of that is visible when it's working. That's rather the point &mdash;
      it's the same care that decides whether a data pipeline still runs
      correctly at 3am in month eleven.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top:var(--space-6);">
      <a href="/demo/">Try the SQL review &rarr;</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp;
      <a href="/contact/">Talk to us about real work &rarr;</a>
    </p>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
